# Cursor model rule (Zak, Nov 7, 2026)

- Never use a Fast variant of any model. Fast is always off.
- Composer: repeat or simple jobs only (small copy or style fixes, rules files, running existing tests). Never the final reviewer of a real feature.
- Grok 4.7 Medium: normal builds and their final QA.
- Grok 4.7 High: hard builds (tricky bugs, payments, shared code). No need to ask Zak first.
- Every launch names its model explicitly. Never rely on the account default.
- Every bot tells Zak which model it is using for each Cursor task.
- No Opus or Sonnet unless Zak OKs that specific review.

Source of truth: Cursor Build Rules doc
